A||||6||la9||If you are thinking of rebuilding a V6||||1||
Z||000000||la9||01-02-2000||07:36 PM||||I just got the bottom end of my engine back and if you are thinking of doing it yourself I'd say figure $1500 into your budget. This will only apply if I do not need new valves. I don't have the heads back yet. I know some will say you can do it cheaper and they are right, but I did everything the right way though thus the higher price. I did have it balanced which everyone has there own opinion on that. I also had the cam and main bearings line-honed which I think is worth it. I have all new parts in the bottom end from top of the line manufacturers. Plus you will need to figure in a lot of your time. On the plus side, I know what is in my engine, I'm having the transmission rebuilt while it is out, I repainted the engine cradle, switched to poly bushings, and changed the motor&transmission mounts. Things that don't get done when someone else does the work. So if you think you are going to save money doing it yourself, think twice.<BR>Also don't forget about the last bolt in every asembly that doesn't come out.<P>Just some advice for someone thinking they can do it cheaper. The other thing I did was have the shortblock assembled. For $75 I figured it would save a lot of arguing if the crank snaps in half, he can't say it was because I didn't torque everything right. Cheap insurance in my book.||||reg||1
Z||000001||GREENDANO||01-03-2000||06:20 PM||||I wish that was the case with machine shop warranties.  Once you fire the engine, it's yours.  I developed a rod knock on my big block AFTER spending $2100 in machine work to make everything right.  That happened 500 miles into the new engine.  I had them put the lower half together the first time at my expense like you're suggesting.  Their answer after I took the motor back, "This is how much it is going to cost you....."  You don't get any extra insurance if they put it together, only a lighter wallet.  <BR>  I've asked around and usually this is standard practice.  <BR>If you want a warrenty, get an assembled long block.  ||||reg||4
Z||000002||Cooter||01-03-2000||09:27 PM||||Dan-0<BR>I had a similiar incident on my 'Burb's first 454. I had the block align honed and installed a new crank, bearings etc from the guy who did the machine work. His exact words were, "That thing will go for another 100,000 miles. I did it right." <BR>Well, 10,000 miles into this engine it broke the crankshaft and all I got was a "I sure do hate that." The next time I built a completly different block with steel crank and it has 25,000 miles of hard use with no problems. Just because someone says that do it right and will back it up, does not mean they will.||||reg||1
Z||000003||la9||01-05-2000||02:48 AM||||You guys sure know how to make a guy who has just spent a boatload of time and money on a car he's never driven feel really good. I did get a 3 month warranty on the shortblock if that means anything.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Steven||01-05-2000||04:53 PM||||I hate to be the one to say it, but that 3 months started when you picked it up, not from when it is started for the first time. Just thought you might want to keep that in mind.||||reg||1
Z||000005||GREENDANO||01-05-2000||09:25 PM||||Taking into account any major part failures, if you had the correct machine work done, the clearances are on the money and you're confident with your assembly, then you shouldn't have problems.  My BB that popped was a 500 HP Pro-street motor that was tweaked to it's limit.  It's not like it was on borrowed time, but I think the old saying "Speed costs, How fast can you afford to go?"  applies here.<BR>  Dan-O<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||la9||01-06-2000||02:23 AM||||Believe it or not I told the guy it would be awhile before I got it back together and he gave me an extra 2 months on the warranty. 5 months total in writing. So he must have confidence in his work or he is one of those guys that just isn't going to care when I come back with a problem. I just rebuilt the 2.8 stock except for the cam and some porting so I'm hoping it will all turn out OK.||||reg||1
